The "Everything Shop" project has been a comprehensive exercise in full-stack web application development. Throughout this course, we have successfully navigated the entire software development lifecycle, from requirements elicitation and system design to implementation and verification.

*Key Achievements:*
1. *Architecture Mastery*: We successfully implemented a Monolithic MVC architecture, establishing a clean separation of concerns between our Postgres data layer, Express logic layer, and React presentation layer.
2. *Technology Proficiency*: The project demonstrates solid competence in the PERN stack, leveraging TypeScript for type safety and Prisma for efficient database interactions.
3. *Educational Value*: Beyond the code, this project provided invaluable insights into state management, authenticating users securely with JWT, and handling complex object relationships (e.g., Sellers owning Products which are in Customers' Orders).

By delivering a functioning, containerized application, we have met the primary objectives of the course and laid a strong foundation for future software engineering endeavors.
